ine","Trajan","Nero"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":"Constantine","explanation":"It was believed to portray the Christian emperor Constantine rather than a pagan ruler.","format":"context_relation","references":[{"file":"Editorial reference: Equestrian Statue of Marcus Aurelius","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equestrian_statue_of_Marcus_Aurelius"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","version":"editorial-v80","editorialStatus74":"ready","skill74":"context_relation","topic74":"Equestrian Statue of Marcus Aurelius","difficulty74":"unrated","testedFactKeys":["equestrian statue of marcus aurelius|reception|constantine"],"alphaLineage":[119],"relevanceReason":"Extends Art History knowledge using an Alpha-benchmarked context_relation format; no claim of official exam prediction.","reviewStatus":"approved","lineage74":"Original study question; domain and task benchmarked against AlphaTest. Not an official exam question.","evidence":{"type":"source-checked","checkedAt":"2026-10-05","sourceTextSha256":"6c65087efecf2abce7a9431122b0d300e8b1475e77f979f5085954dc22c1c933","review":"Source passage, answer, distractors and existing-bank relationship review; not statistically calibrated."},"fingerprint":"9e4410b343d2215279ed"},{"id":"GEN43-Q03719","qid":3719,"nodeId":"ORIGINAL80-3719","relatedNodeIds":["ORIGINAL80-3719"],"factIds":["ORIGINAL80-3719"],"major":"Art History","group":"Donatello","stem":"Donatello's bronze David is notable as a Renaissance revival of which form?","choices":["Freestanding male nude","Architectural caryatid","Ivory triptych","Colossal equestrian group","Painted wooden crucifix"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":"Freestanding male nude","explanation":"The bronze statue revived the freestanding nude male figure associated with antiquity.","format":"classification_style","references":[{"file":"Editorial reference: Donatello","page":null,"verificationUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donatello"}],"examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope